Pokemon scarlet and violet are finally  out and they Mark a number of changes  for the mainline series here are 15 ways  to make the most of your time in paldea  number one go to school nerd yes Pokemon  scarlet and violet let you attend  classes take tests and befriend your  teachers there's nothing stopping you  from cutting class but completing  classes will earn you some nice rewards  like experienced candies  to enroll in a class just talk to this  lady at the front desk and you're good  to go it's worth revisiting the school  often because you will unlock new  classes as you progress who knows you  might actually learn something as well  number two go anywhere once you've made  it through the tutorial you are free to  roam paldea in its entirety however  there is no level scaling across paldea  this means that some areas will be way  too tough for you at the beginning I  still like to poke around some of these  high level areas but don't expect to  accomplish much if your Pokemon are too  low level the general rule of thumb is  that the further you get from a sagoza  the tougher gyms trainers and wild  Pokemon will be since mazagoza is on the  southern tip that means the toughest  areas will be to the north  [Music]  number three the map considering how big  paldea is you will probably spend a lot  of time looking at the map unfortunately  the map isn't great you cannot rotate  the map when it is fully zoomed out but  it's the only way you can see the  entirety of paldea meanwhile zooming in  all the way is the only way you can see  all the different shops and there are  lots of different shops  [Music]  number four Pokedex rewards like every  Pokemon game your ultimate goal is to  complete the Pokedex Pokemon scarlet and  violet gives you rewards for hitting  certain Milestones to claim those  rewards open your Pokedex and press X  for every 10 volumes you will get items  ranging from pokeballs to XP candies  goodbye fly  scarlet and violet has fast travel and  it's available very early on once you  find a Pokemon Center you can fly there  easy as that keep in mind that you can't  fast travel while indoors if you try  Oak's famous words will echo through  your head there's a time and place for  everything but not now  [Music]  number six hello Glide you might be able  to go anywhere in paldea but it's pretty  tough to get anywhere efficiently  without meridon or corydon's traversal  ability in order to unlock these you'll  want to hunt down and defeat Titan  Pokemon in the path of Legends questline  cloth is the easiest to defeat and  you'll get a speed boost ability however  I started with a different Titan and  managed to unlock surf at the very  beginning of the game  number seven free-fallen paldea is home  to some tall mountains and deep Canyons  fortunately for you there's no fall  damage if something catches your  interest deep in a ravine just walk  right off the ledge if you fell by  accident you can press Y and you'll be  warped back up to the cliff you fell  from  [Music]  number eight battle trainers it's true  locking eyes with another trainer won't  initiate a battle in Pokemon scarlet and  violet however it's still important to  battle trainers when you find them at  some Pokemon centers you can find a  league representative once you've  defeated a certain number of trainers in  a specified area they will give you a  reward usually in the form of a TM these  trainers aren't too hard to find so just  explore each area you visit thoroughly  and you should be fine  [Music]  number nine to rasterize Pokemon scarlet  and violet introduces a new battle  mechanic called terastalizing basically  every Pokemon in paldea has a terror  type some have terror types different  from their original typing when they  terastalize their typing can change you  can drasticize one Pokemon once after  healing your Pokemon up at a Pokemon  Center so use this mechanic sparingly  [Music]  number 10 Auto battles Auto battling is  new to scarlet and violet and it comes  with some advantages and disadvantages  let's start with the positives Auto  battles are quick and net you a reduced  amount of experience if you want to  quickly level up a Pokemon the best way  to do that is to find an area with  Pokemon that are slightly higher levels  than yours and make sure you have a type  advantage against them tap the R button  near some Pokemon and the first monster  in your party will clear them out the  downside of Auto battles is that most  pokemon won't evolve and new moves  automatically get filed away in your  Pokemon's move pool of course if you  missed the evolution window it will  still evolve next level up just make  sure it levels up from a regular battle  or rare candies the other constant fear  I have when it comes to Auto battling is  accidentally knocking out a Shiny  Pokemon if you see one press ZR to  recall your Pokemon and approach it  normally  number 11 surprise wild Pokemon although  you can't catch Pokemon in scarlet and  violet without triggering a battle you  can still surprise them and get an extra  turn the B button will let you crouch  and you can use ZL to lock on and ZR to  send out the first Pokemon in your party  doing this can also make it easier to  catch wild Pokemon  [Music]  number 12 move pools thankfully if a  Pokemon does luna move through Auto  battling you can relearn it by checking  the Pokemon summary page in the menu  every move of Pokemon has learned can be  swapped out on the Fly this includes TMS  if you've taught them some in the past  number 13 TM crafting Pokemon scarlet  and violet introduced TM crafting in  order to craft a TM you need crafting  components which can be found by  defeating Pokemon and Lake points which  you should earn plenty of as you  progress basically any TM you found  automatically becomes craftable as long  as you have the right parts  number 14 picnics picnics are also new  to scarlet and violet and they allow you  to feed your Pokemon sandwiches you can  set up a picnic basically anywhere and  make sandwiches as long as you have all  the required ingredients sandwiches can  increase your odds of catching specific  Pokemon spawn more eggs and even  increase your shiny odds  number 15 breeding speaking of picnics  breeding has been overhauled in scarlet  and violet now in order to get eggs you  need to have two compatible Pokemon in  your party and start a picnic if they  are compatible eggs will spawn in the  picnic basket on the ground over time  any eggs you collect will automatically  transfer to your Pokemon boxes it's  worth mentioning that there's still a  lot we don't know about breeding so do  some research on your own when more  information is available I plan on  revisiting this in a future video so  make sure to subscribe down below  there you have it those are 15 tips that  should get you started in Pokemon  scarlet and violet stay tuned to  Gamespot for more coverage  [Music]
 

